{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This developer guide describes how to sync data between the main app and its keyboard."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit makes it easy to sync data between the main app and its keyboard extension, by setting up an App Group and adding that information to your ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Step-1-Create-an-App-Group","text":"Step 1. Create an App Group"},{"numberOfColumns":2,"type":"row","columns":[{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"developer-data-sync-developer-portal","type":"image"}]}]},{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First create a new App Group in the Apple Developer Portal, under Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select Identifiers and tap the plus button to add a new App Group with the name “group.<your-apps-bundle-id>”."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An macOS App Group must start with the Team ID instead of “group.”. This means that iOS & macOS use different groups."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important"}]}]},{"text":"Step 2. Enable the App Group","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-2-Enable-the-App-Group","level":2},{"type":"row","columns":[{"size":1,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"developer-data-sync-xcode-app"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"size":1,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Second, enable the App Group for both your app and its keyboard extension, under “Signing & Capabilites”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s very important to enable the App Group for all targets that need access to the shared data."}]}],"name":"Important"}]}],"numberOfColumns":2},{"text":"Step 3. Set up KeyboardKit","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-3-Set-up-KeyboardKit","level":2},{"type":"row","columns":[{"size":1,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"developer-data-sync-keyboard-app"}]}]},{"size":1,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lastly, add the App Group ID to your "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". This will tell KeyboardKit to use an App Group synced settings store.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"tip","name":"Tip","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Getting-Started-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" guide shows how to set up the main app and its keyboard extension with an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"numberOfColumns":2},{"anchor":"Manual-Setup-Optional","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Manual Setup (Optional)"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you don’t want to use a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to set up data syncing across all targets, you can set up the shared ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardSettings","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" store manually as well, for instance to a custom ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Foundation\/UserDefaults","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instance that is configured to sync data in a way that fits your needs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you set up data sync manually, you must make sure that the settings store is configured in both the main app and the keyboard.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Articles"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Settings-Article"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Settings-Article"]]},"metadata":{"images":[{"identifier":"Developer-Article-Data-Syncing.jpg","type":"card"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}],"title":"Data Syncing","color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"purple"}},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-data-syncing"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Developer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Custom-Keyboards","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Debugging","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Dictation","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-dSYMs","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Experiments","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Memory-Management","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Themes"],"title":"Developer"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/